### Settings.

## Which operation was refused: the first word of the error.

settings-what-settings = settings

## Why a setting was not written, or a change of settings not undone or
## made again. The setting is named as git lists it.

# What git wrote when it refused.
settings-not-taken-away = { $key } could not be taken away: { $stderr }
# The setting's name, quoted (at most its first 80 characters).
settings-not-writable = { $key } is not a setting that can be written
settings-not-as-left = { $key } is not what this action left it as; nothing was changed
